      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-13T04:19:38Z"
      },
      "message": "test(setup): pin that undoing DeleteSetup keeps the setup order and the posted program\n\nThe setup order is the name order (setup::setups sorts by name); nothing\nstores a position, so a setup re-spawned by undo sorts back into its old\nplace. The report came from PR #1361's test, whose \"Front\"/\"Back\" pair was\nalready in name order [\"Back\", \"Front\"] before the delete.\n\nNew suite setup_delete_order: delete the middle of three setups, undo,\nand assert the setup names, the operation order and the full posted\nG-code text against the pre-delete program; redo and undo again. A second\ntest deletes the first setup (the one None resolves to) and asserts it\ncomes back first.\n\nFixes #1362\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
